@startuml sequence-send-invoice

!include sequence-styling.puml.inc

actor "Office Manager" as OfficeManager
participant "little-trotter-invoice" as WebApp
database "PostgreSQL\n<size:10>[Database]</size>" as DB
queue "NATS JetStream\n<size:10>[Stream: document-jobs]</size>" as JobQueue
participant "kotlin-xpdf" as Renderer
database "RustFS\n<size:10>[Object Store]</size>" as S3 <<storage>>
queue "NATS JetStream\n<size:10>[Stream: document-job-results]</size>" as ResultQueue

OfficeManager -> WebApp: click "Send"
WebApp -> DB: persist GenerationJob\n(trigger=SEND, issued=true, PENDING)
WebApp --> OfficeManager: send requested\n(invoice stays IN_REVIEW)
WebApp -> JobQueue: publish job
JobQueue -> Renderer: render + validate e-invoice
Renderer -> S3: store documents
Renderer -> ResultQueue: publish result
ResultQueue -> WebApp: deliver result
WebApp -> DB: mark job COMPLETED/FAILED

alt job COMPLETED and validation VALID
  WebApp -> WebApp: resolveSendOutcome:\ntransition(id, ISSUED)
  WebApp -> DB: stamp date, freeze payment term,\nassign number, flip status
  WebApp --> OfficeManager: push status: ISSUED
else job FAILED, or COMPLETED but INVALID/UNAVAILABLE
  WebApp -> DB: message-center entry\n(invoice unchanged)
  WebApp --> OfficeManager: push notification: send failed
end

note over OfficeManager, WebApp
  Manual escalation, not part of the automated flow above: if validation resolved
  UNAVAILABLE (the validation tooling itself was unreachable, not a data defect),
  the Office Manager may still send with an audited override reason — the pre-existing
  FinalizationGate override, reusing the already-COMPLETED job's document; the
  same call the Invoice Lifecycle State Machine's IN_REVIEW -> ISSUED edge always
  used before this feature. INVALID/PENDING/NOT_VALIDATED remain non-overridable.
end note

$SequenceStorageLegend()
@enduml
